  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: db176a60e3b58b4408636b22a97519c4, type: 3}
  m_Name: EquipmentMalfunctionEvent
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::MarsEvent
  eventTitle: Equipment Malfunction
  eventDescription: Warning! A critical maintenance system at the Mars outpost has
    malfunctioned, reducing the effectiveness of the habitat's protective equipment.
    The crew must decide whether to perform an immediate repair or activate an emergency
    maintenance protocol to keep the base operational.
  targetSol: 6
  optionATitle: Repair Protective Equipment
  energyChangeA: -12
  lifeSupportChangeA: 0
  shieldChangeA: 18
  resultTitleA: Protective Equipment Repaired
  resultDescriptionA: The crew successfully repairs the habitat's protective equipment.
    Shield integrity improves, increasing the base's resistance to environmental
    hazards. However, the repair requires a significant amount of energy.
  optionBTitle: Activate Emergency Maintenance
  energyChangeB: -5
  lifeSupportChangeB: -8
  shieldChangeB: 8
  resultTitleB: Emergency Maintenance Activated
  resultDescriptionB: The emergency maintenance protocol restores part of the habitat's
    protective capacity. The operation requires less energy than a complete repair,
    but redirects resources from life support systems, temporarily reducing their
    efficiency.
  educationalExplanation: Space exploration requires reliable equipment and regular
    maintenance. Extreme temperatures, dust, radiation, and mechanical wear can affect
    spacecraft and habitat systems. Engineers design space equipment with redundancy,
    monitoring systems, and maintenance procedures to reduce the risk of critical
    failures during long-duration missions.
  scientificSource: "NASA \u2014 Human Spaceflight"
  scientificSourceURL: https://www.nasa.gov/humans-in-space/
